        "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]?$",
        "worked_solution": "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =1{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(-1){x}_{1}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+(-1){x}_{3}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}{x}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({x}_{1}-{x}_{3})+{x}_{2}(3{x}_{3})+{x}_{3}(-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}{x}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
